#N canvas 30 30 2300 1600 12;
#X text 20 20 u_store -- a KEYED LINE STORE with one file behind it. Give it a list \, it replaces the line whose FIRST ATOM matches and appends if there is none. Tell it write and it writes its file \; tell it load and it reads the file into a SEPARATE text and replays every line out outlet 1 -- the live store is never wiped by a load. It knows nothing about policy \, about WHEN to write \, or about the state bus -- u_state owns all three., f 58;
#X text 920 20 creation arg 1: the FULL PATH of its file \, absolute. inlet 1: a LIST to store \, or write \, or load. outlet 1: each stored line \, one message per line \, replayed by load. outlet 2: a bang whenever a line changed \, which is what u_state's dirty flag hangs off., f 58;
#X text 1620 20 IT EXISTS BECAUSE THERE ARE TWO OF IT. auto and manual are the same store with different write policies \, and ref-conventions.md says anything you would copy is an abstraction rather than a duplicated subpatch -- two copies are two codebases that diverge silently., f 58;
#X obj 20 320 inlet;
#X obj 20 380 route write load;
#X obj 20 460 t b;
#X obj 20 520 symbol \$1;
#X msg 20 570 write -c \$1;
#X obj 620 460 t b b;
#X obj 900 520 symbol \$1;
#X msg 900 570 read -c \$1;
#X obj 620 640 t b b;
#X msg 800 700 0;
#X obj 620 760 text size \$0-f;
#X obj 620 820 until;
#X obj 620 880 f;
#X obj 620 940 t f f;
#X obj 820 1000 + 1;
#X obj 620 1060 text get \$0-f;
#X obj 620 1200 outlet;
#X obj 1180 460 list append;
#X obj 1180 520 t b l l;
#X obj 1520 590 list split 1;
#X obj 1520 650 text search \$0-t;
#X obj 1520 710 moses 0;
#X obj 1520 780 t b;
#X obj 1520 840 text size \$0-t;
#X obj 1180 900 text set \$0-t;
#X obj 960 1200 outlet;
#X obj 20 700 text define \$0-t;
#X text 20 790 THE REJECT OUTLET IS THE DATA. route matches write and load by SELECTOR \, and a list whose first atom is a symbol is neither -- so everything to be STORED falls out of the reject. That is the NORMAL path here rather than an error path \, which is the opposite of how a reject usually reads., f 44;
#X text 20 990 list append IS LOAD-BEARING AND IT WAS MEASURED. text set and text search both answer a bare selector with no method for 'mode'. Seen in this repo twice -- in u_err first \, and again while building this. A message box typed mode compose mode-1 carries mode as its SELECTOR \, not as data., f 44;
#X text 1620 900 text search RETURNS -1 FOR A KEY IT DOES NOT HOLD \, and moses's LEFT outlet carries that -1 rather than a bang -- the reject-outlet rule again. Without the t b it would reach text set's line-number inlet as -1 and Pd would answer line number (-1) < 0 \, which is the exact bug moses caused in u_err's log. So a miss becomes text size instead \, which is one past the end \, which APPENDS. Verified in 0.49 both times., f 58;
#X text 1180 1000 KEYS MATCH WHOLE ATOMS \, NOT PREFIXES -- measured while building this: with lines keyed mode \, drums and drumkit \, a search for drums returns 1 and not 2. So a key may safely be a prefix of another., f 44;
#X text 240 1200 REPLAY IS RESET THEN RUN \, and the reset is the RIGHT outlet so it happens first. text size of an empty text is 0 \, and until with 0 runs ZERO times -- so a file that does not exist replays nothing rather than looping forever. Measured rather than reasoned. text get past the end returns a bang and prints nothing \, so the loop cannot overrun into an error either., f 44;
#X text 1900 460 read -c AND write -c MUST MATCH. Measured: a file written with -c and read back WITHOUT it comes back as ONE line -- text size 1 -- because Pd is hunting for semicolons that are not there. The -c is what keeps the file greppable AND what makes it readable again., f 44;
#X text 1180 1330 THE PATH IS A CREATION ARGUMENT CAPTURED INTO A symbol OBJECT \, because in a MESSAGE box \$1 is the incoming message rather than the argument. That trap has already cost this project a silent MIDI port and a soundfiler write to a table called 0-a0. In an OBJECT box \$1 is the argument \, so symbol \$1 holds the path and the message box below substitutes it in., f 44;
#X obj 900 660 text define \$0-f;
